    "image_with_text_hepztF": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_keQcaw": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Voltage Conversions",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "text_transform": true,
            "mobile_title_size": "normal"
          }
        },
        "text_rawKrW": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<ul><li>Many of our fitness equipment models are cordless (self-powered). Plug-in products offer a voltage upgrade option on our product page.</li><li>The pricing listed for equipment includes the standard 115-120V setup, suitable for North/South America and select countries. Note that most countries in Africa/Asia/Europe require 220-240V. For an additional fee, we can provide or install a transformer that converts your standard 220-240 voltage to the equipment’s required 115-120V setup.</li><li>For treadmills, many of our models offer ample internal space to accommodate an internal transformer, which remains hidden within the unit. This setup is referred to as an \"Internal Transformer.\" On the other hand, most ellipticals, bikes, and steppers are compatible with an external transformer. In this scenario, the machine connects to the transformer, which is typically positioned near the machine or against the wall, with the transformer then plugged into the wall outlet.</li></ul>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "text_size": "middle"
          }
        }
      },
